---
source: crates/pixi_manifest/src/manifests/workspace.rs
expression: "expect_parse_warnings(r#\"\n[workspace]\nname = \"foo\"\nchannels = [{ channel = \"conda-forge\", exclude-newer = \"7d\" }]\nplatforms = []\n\n[exclude-newer]\npolars = \"0d\"\n\n[pypi-exclude-newer]\nboltons = \"0d\"\n\"#)"
---
  ⚠ the top-level `[exclude-newer]` table of per-package cutoffs is deprecated and will be removed in a future release
   ╭─[pixi.toml:7:1]
 6 │
 7 │ ╭─▶ [exclude-newer]
 8 │ ├─▶ polars = "0d"
   · ╰──── this table will be removed
 9 │
   ╰────
  help: set a `cutoff` in `[workspace.exclude-newer]` to replace the zero cutoffs of `polars` with `exemptions`, note that it also applies to the channels without their own `exclude-newer`

  ⚠ the top-level `[pypi-exclude-newer]` table of per-package cutoffs is deprecated and will be removed in a future release
    ╭─[pixi.toml:10:1]
  9 │
 10 │ ╭─▶ [pypi-exclude-newer]
 11 │ ├─▶ boltons = "0d"
    · ╰──── this table will be removed
    ╰────
  help: the zero cutoffs of `boltons` have no effect without a cutoff, remove them
